Mesa takes its C11 threads from the C library of stafeto.
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Copyright (C) 2026 Sergey Subbotin <ssubbotin@gmail.com>

with_c11_threads is on only for Android; without it Mesa builds its own
threads_posix.c, which defines mtx_init, cnd_init, thrd_create, call_once and
tss_create, the names relibc's libc.a defines too, and a static link would
have every one of them twice. The test is the macro __stafeto__ the cross
file defines.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 59d30c8..769b844 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1750,6 +1750,11 @@ if cc.has_function('thrd_create', prefix: '#include <threads.h>')
     # Current only Android's c11 <threads.h> are verified
     pre_args += '-DHAVE_THRD_CREATE'
     with_c11_threads = true
+  elif cc.get_define('__stafeto__') == '1'
+    # stafeto: the C library (relibc) has all of <threads.h>, and the sources
+    # of Mesa's own copy would define the same names a second time.
+    pre_args += '-DHAVE_THRD_CREATE'
+    with_c11_threads = true
   endif
 endif
 
